config UART_PICO_DE_GALLO
	bool "Pico de Gallo UART controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ODP_PICO_DE_GALLO_UART_ENABLED
	depends on ARCH_POSIX
	select SERIAL
	select SERIAL_HAS_DRIVER
	help
	  Enable the Pico de Gallo UART controller driver. This driver forwards
	  Zephyr UART API calls to a Pico de Gallo USB bridge attached to the
	  host running native_sim via the Pico de Gallo C FFI.

	  Polling only. The asynchronous and interrupt-driven UART APIs are not
	  supported: the driver deliberately does not select
	  SERIAL_SUPPORT_ASYNC, SERIAL_SUPPORT_INTERRUPT or
	  SERIAL_SUPPORT_WIDE_DATA. Those symbols are global and another driver
	  in the same build may enable the corresponding API; this driver ships
	  side-effect-free stubs for the resulting callback slots so that such a
	  build fails loudly rather than dereferencing a NULL slot.

	  The controller is thread-context-only. Every operation that reaches
	  hardware is a blocking USB round trip, so no callback may be invoked
	  from an ISR or before the kernel is up. Those contexts are rejected
	  before any mutex is taken and before any FFI call is made: polling
	  input returns -1, polling output drops the character and increments a
	  dropped counter, and the remaining integer callbacks return
	  -EWOULDBLOCK in an ISR and -EAGAIN pre-kernel.

	  Reconfiguration is not atomic. The firmware's set_baudrate restores an
	  enabled UARTCR before returning, so there is a brief window in which
	  the new divisor is in effect while the old framing still applies.
	  Bytes already sitting in the firmware ring were decoded under the old
	  framing and cannot be told apart from new ones, and more may still
	  arrive after the driver clears its local staging. Callers must quiesce
	  and drain both directions before calling uart_configure().

	  The device cannot serve as an early console. It initializes at
	  POST_KERNEL, whereas the CONFIG_EARLY_CONSOLE hook installs at
	  PRE_KERNEL_1 and checks device readiness first, so the hook would
	  simply not be installed. Selecting this instance as the chosen
	  zephyr,console with CONFIG_EARLY_CONSOLE enabled is rejected at build
	  time.

if UART_PICO_DE_GALLO

config UART_PICO_DE_GALLO_INIT_PRIORITY
	int "Pico de Gallo UART controller initialization priority"
	default 50
	help
	  POST_KERNEL initialization priority of the Pico de Gallo UART
	  controller.

	  It must be greater than CONFIG_MFD_PICO_DE_GALLO_INIT_PRIORITY
	  (default 40): this controller borrows the host connection owned by its
	  odp,pico-de-gallo MFD parent, so the parent has to be ready first.
	  It shares the default 50 with the I2C and SPI controllers, which it
	  does not depend on.

	  Kconfig cannot check the arithmetic. Runtime readiness is
	  authoritative instead: an inverted priority makes initialization
	  return -ENODEV rather than using a parent that is not yet open.

endif # UART_PICO_DE_GALLO
